Every HotLoop product is under the HotLoop Source License Agreement 1.0 below: HotLoop IoT, HotLoop Edge, HotLoop Gateway, HotLoop Edge Relay, HotLoop Flow, HotLoop Cascade, HotLoop for CODESYS, HotLoop Transmitter, Spark SDK and Spark Manager. A version that was released under an earlier license stays under that license.

**Licensor:** HotLoop LLC

**Licensed Work:** HotLoop IoT, HotLoop Edge, HotLoop Gateway, HotLoop Edge Relay, HotLoop Flow, HotLoop Cascade, HotLoop for CODESYS, HotLoop Transmitter, Spark SDK and Spark Manager, in the version of each that you received. The Licensed Work is (c) 2026 HotLoop LLC.

## 1. What you may always do

You may copy, modify, create derivative works of, and redistribute the Licensed Work, and use it for any purpose that is not production use.

## 2. Production use

You may make production use of the Licensed Work in these three ways, and only these three.

(1) Home and Lab Use. You may use the Licensed Work for personal, household, hobby, non-commercial, educational, evaluation, development and testing purposes. Evaluation, development and testing count as Home and Lab Use only while the Licensed Work is not running, monitoring or controlling live operations of a business.

(2) Education, Nonprofit and Government Use. If you are an Educational Institution, a Nonprofit Organization or a Government Body, you may use the Licensed Work for your own operations and mission, anywhere, without running it through EmberNet. You may have a contractor install and operate the Licensed Work for you, on equipment you own or control.

(3) Use through EmberNet. Any use of the Licensed Work that you run through EmberNet (https://embernet.ai), including Business Use, is unrestricted. Sections 4 and 6 do not apply to it.

## 3. Definitions

"Educational Institution" means a school, college, university or other institution that is accredited or licensed by a government authority or a recognized accrediting body to provide education.

"Nonprofit Organization" means an organization that is organized and operated as a nonprofit under the law of the place where it is organized, whose net earnings do not benefit any private owner or member, and that is recognized as tax-exempt or as a charity in that place.

"Government Body" means a national, state, provincial, regional, local or tribal government, or an agency, department or public authority of one, acting in its governmental capacity. A company that a government owns and that sells goods or services for profit is not a Government Body.

Each of the three is the institution itself. A for-profit subsidiary, affiliate or spin-off of an Educational Institution, a Nonprofit Organization or a Government Body is not one, and neither is a for-profit business that serves one.

"Business Use" means any use by, for or on behalf of a company, partnership, sole proprietorship or other for-profit organization, or in the course of earning a living, to run, monitor, control or support its operations, facilities, products or services. It is Business Use whether the use is purely internal or reaches customers, and whether or not a fee is charged. Use that is not Home and Lab Use and is not covered by section 2(2) is Business Use.

"Run it through EmberNet" means that each copy of the Licensed Work is deployed and operated under an EmberNet account. The account may be the account of the organization the Licensed Work is operated for, or the account of a systems integrator that installs and operates it for that organization. Either one is acceptable. A "systems integrator" is a business that installs, configures and operates the Licensed Work for its customers on equipment or in cloud accounts that the customer owns or controls. A systems integrator may charge for its own services, such as installation, configuration and support, but not for the Licensed Work itself or for access to it.

## 4. What is not allowed

Outside EmberNet, this license does not let you: (a) offer the Licensed Work, or any of its functionality, to third parties as a hosted, managed or software-as-a-service offering; (b) sell, resell, sublicense, rent or lease the Licensed Work; (c) embed or bundle the Licensed Work in a product or service that you sell, license or otherwise provide for a fee, except as section 5 allows; or (d) charge anyone for access to the Licensed Work.

## 5. Spark SDK and HotLoop Transmitter

Spark SDK and HotLoop Transmitter exist to be built into things you make. You may build the Spark SDK files that HotLoop supplies into your own firmware, and you may include the HotLoop Transmitter library in your own PLC projects, and you may deliver or sell the resulting firmware and projects in compiled form to your customers. What you deliver must be your own product. It must not be the Spark SDK or the HotLoop Transmitter library itself, or a toolkit made of them, and you may not hand over their files as files.

## 6. Any other use

Any use not allowed by sections 1, 2 and 5 needs a separate commercial license from the Licensor. To ask for one, email support@hotloop.io.

## 7. Copies and derivative works

Every copy of the Licensed Work, modified or not, and every derivative work stays under this license, and you must include this license with it. Anyone who receives the Licensed Work from you is bound by this license.

## 8. Termination

If you use the Licensed Work in violation of this license, your rights under it end automatically, for this version and every other version of the Licensed Work.

